      "defect": "citation-inaccurate",
      "evidence": "The cited thm-ftc-first-part states that the integral function of an integrable function is differentiable at its continuity points, and consequently is a primitive when the integrand is continuous. It does not state the reverse identity for an arbitrary C^1 function g, namely g(v)-g(u)=∫_u^v g'(s) ds. [F5] attributes that identity to the dependency, and Proof step 2.1 uses it to integrate a differential inequality. The identity is true here but requires the Newton–Leibniz direction or a separate derivation; this citation does not license it.",
